This license covers every file in the `ee/` folder of the Dinghy repository (the "Software").
It does not cover any file outside that folder. Those files are under the licenses named in
the repository's LICENSE-NOTICE.md.

1. What you may do. You may read, copy and change the Software, and run it, for development
   and testing only. For example, you may run its tests, try a change on your own computer, or
   send a patch to the Dinghy project.

2. Running Dinghy with the cloud features off. You may also run the unmodified Software in
   production, as part of Dinghy, as long as the cloud features stay off. They stay off when
   none of the settings STRIPE_SECRET_KEY, STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET, STRIPE_PRICE_ID and
   CLOUD_SIGNUP is set. This is how every self-hosted install runs, and it needs no agreement.

3. What needs an agreement. Any other use in production needs a written agreement with
   OnceByte, LLC that allows it. That includes turning on the cloud features, running a changed
   copy of the Software in production, and offering the cloud features to others as a service.
   Hosting Dinghy for others with the cloud features off is allowed under section 2.
   "Production" means any use beyond development and testing. Without that agreement, you may
   not do any of these.

4. Your changes. A changed copy of the Software, and any work made from it, is under this same
   license.

5. No other rights. This license grants no other rights, whether by implication or otherwise.
   It grants no right to use the names or trademarks of OnceByte, LLC or Dinghy.

6. Third-party code. Code from others that the Software uses stays under its own license.

7. No warranty. THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR
